ut only having images with no written explanation on what to actually do is=
 extremely unhelpful. It's best to have words to describe what needs to be =
done step by step, and images to show visually what the end result should l=
ook like. Another issue I have with this particular set of instructions is =
that is has both the steps and parts labeled with letters, which is confusi=
ng at first glance.<br><br>2. Looking at not only this post, but many of th=
e others as well, I have learned that the best way to help users is to have=
 clear and organized instructions. First, writing should be consistent and =
use simple language to avoid confusion. Next, illustrations should show acc=
urate orientation, scale, and part placement. Then, parts and steps should =
both be labeled, parts being labeled with letters and steps being labeled w=
ith numbers to avoid confusion. Finally, if the instructions are going to b=
e translated into another language be sure to hire a professional translato=
