<span class=3D"post_mention"><span>This tweet: "Gee thanks bookshelf assemb=
ly instructions, I would have never known that damage done to the parts wou=
ld result in damage" I love how this image states, "Do not use power tools =
to assemble your furniture. Power tools may damage the parts and result in =
damage. It's not so much about how frustrating it is, but rather how frustr=
ated the past installers of a similar product that has me wondering how man=
y times did the company get calls from people about this before the warning=
 was introduced. It reminds me of the incredibly dumb warnings you may find=
 on shop tools in a woodwork or metal work shop. First one that comes to mi=
nd is "Grabbing saw while in motion may cause injury and loss of hands." Ye=
s, I have actually seen a warning like this in multiple wood and metal shop=
s. Sometimes I have seen it posted up on the wall for giggles.</span></span=
></p>
<p>2. At most I can use this lesson to remind myself that these dumb common=
 sense rules and warnings exist because there where some idiotic unfortunat=
e souls that actually did these things. Just reminds me that, for many peop=
le, common sense just is not common anymore.</p></span></div><span dir=3D"l=
