<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Many of the examples I saw posted were just badly translated manuals. Gr=
anted, those are indeed&nbsp;<em>bad user help</em>, but you might imagine =
that the instructions were perfectly clear in the original language.</p>
<p>In this example, it seems like the authors forgot to finish what they we=
re writing. "a template would have been helpful" =E2=80=94 it reads like th=
ere's a second writer putting a suggestion in the original writer's guide, =
and nobody went back to remove it &amp; write what was needed.</p>
<p>When I write instructions at work or online, I always triple check my wr=
iting before sending it off. Even then, I still often make edits after I'm =
done. In a manual though, these kinds of mistakes aren't something that can=
 be fixed after the fact, so it makes sense for multiple other eyes to look=
 through the whole document to find incomplete instructions.</p></span></di=
