resource-type=3D"discussion_topic.reply" data-resource-id=3D"2299815"><p>I =
chose a tweet about an instruction manual with only pictures and a lack of =
words:</p>
<p><span class=3D"post_mention"><img src=3D"https://uah.instructure.com/use=
rs/30724/files/9936227/preview?hidden=3D1&amp;verifier=3D0rpoZRBOwZR1USEq0R=
tc1uLaHq08ggDYy2hlIVu3" alt=3D"module-4-discussion-useless-assistance-scree=
nshot.png" width=3D"338" height=3D"271" data-api-endpoint=3D"https://uah.in=
structure.com/api/v1/users/30724/files/9936227" data-api-returntype=3D"File=
"></span></p>
<p><span class=3D"post_mention">1. Due to a lack of written instructions, t=
he user will have difficulty with following just picture-based instructions=
. The pictures are also out of context, with close-ups not showing exactly =
where the components are located on the product. The illustration of moveme=
nts and gestures through the use of arrows and hands are also vague. It is =
confusing which component the hands are clasping and what part connects to =
what other part, such as connecting the handle to the main body. There are =
also additional details that seem uselss or convoluted, such as the "volume=
" symbol which has no context for which the noise is supposed to be represe=
nting. The tweet also complains about the size of the manual and the waste =
of space on each page. Clearly, the manual could have used some written ins=
tructions, have better context for the images, and be more space-efficient =
with the instructions so as not to waste paper.</span></p>
<p><span class=3D"post_mention">2. I've learned that images alone are not e=
nough for helping a user along. Images should be additive to user help rath=
er than the sole aspect of user help. Additionally, it would be helpful to =
add numbers, names, and/or color-coding to each component of a product so t=
hat it helps the user identify the parts. Each image should also be a wider=
-shot picture with zoom-in circles to show where exactly the pictured compo=
nent is on the product. Lastly, the size of the manual should be taken into=
 consideration and space should be utilized efficiently in order to use les=
s paper material.</span></p></span></div><span dir=3D"ltr" data-testid=3D"p=
ost-message-container" class=3D"css-1pu4tqw-view--block"><div dir=3D"ltr" c=
