=3D"2299778"><ol style=3D"list-style-type: decimal;">
<li>One tweet that really struck me was from Millie Rocklage, who wrote, =
=E2=80=9CShe LOVES the Barbie Dreamhouse so it was worth it, but holy smoke=
s it was a pain to assemble with the instructions provided!=E2=80=9D. I=E2=
=80=99ve been there myself multiple times. Just eager to build something fu=
n, only to find the =E2=80=9Chelp=E2=80=9D is a wall of tiny text, unclear =
illustrations, and no logical sequence.</li>
<li>I've felt that same frustration rising when dealing with software or de=
vices. You follow the guide step by step, only to hit a wall because the in=
structions are outdated, incomplete, or poorly organized. It's doubly upset=
ting when you encounter identical issues across different products from the=
 same company. At that point, it's not just an oversight, it=E2=80=99s just=
 negligence. I would fix this by giving numbered, bite-sized steps paired w=
ith clear, call-out diagrams. I would also have multiple formats be support=
ed (print, online, video) and have early-user testing be carried out to get=
 rid of any ambiguity before the product is introduced.</li>
</ol></span></div><span dir=3D"ltr" data-testid=3D"post-message-container" =
